.TH AETHER-RULES 1 "October 2026" "Aether 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aether-rules \- inspect, validate, and test custom YARA threat detection rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aether rules
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBrules\fR subcommand provides management and validation utilities for custom YARA signatures. When Aether is compiled with YARA-X support, it loads rules from system and user directories in addition to its embedded core ruleset.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all currently loaded embedded and custom YARA rules, including rule identifiers, severity, and MITRE ATT&CK mappings.
.TP
.B validate \fIPATH\fR
Compile and validate YARA rules located in the specified file or directory. Checks syntax, variable definitions, and regular expression safety without executing scans.
.TP
.B test \fIPATH\fR \fITARGET\fR
Execute a dry-run test of rule compilation and matching against a designated target file.
.SH RULE DIRECTORIES
.TP
.I /etc/aether/rules/
System-wide directory for administrator-provided \fI*.yar\fR and \fI*.yara\fR rule files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/aether/rules/
User-specific directory for custom YARA rules in unprivileged mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaether\fR(1), \fBaether-scan\fR(1), \fBaether-ack\fR(1)
.SH AUTHORS
Aether Security Engineering Team.
